# Bounded integration Wiki handoff

## Authority and procedure reuse

Use only within an assigned accepted integration unit after dependent repairs
and their handoffs settle code. The Commit Supervisor owns the coverage packet,
assigns one bounded leaf editor, and separately commissions fresh read-only
documentation review. Neither editor nor reviewer launches the full manual Wiki
Supervisor or its broader delegation tree. This is integration procedure reuse,
not a claim that a manual Wiki Update run occurred. Builders retain only their
own fresh clean-room-reviewer permission under the SPEC review gate.

Resolve the assigned absolute Wiki home and actual source checkout separately.
Read their current instructions and full local [Wiki session contract](../../../../../Wiki/.agents/wiki-session-contract.md),
[Research](../../../../../Wiki/.agents/skills/wiki-research/SKILL.md),
[Repair](../../../../../Wiki/.agents/skills/wiki-repair/SKILL.md) and
[Audit](../../../../../Wiki/.agents/skills/wiki-audit/SKILL.md) procedures. Reuse
their bounded evidence, article and integrity methods; their manual worker
hierarchies do not override this integration's leaf/delegation boundaries.
Read [Style Guide](../../../../../Wiki/000-Wiki_Guidance/001-Style_Guide/PAGE.md),
[Updating Wiki Content](../../../../../Wiki/000-Wiki_Guidance/003-Updating_Wikis/PAGE.md)
and [Audit Workflow](../../../../../Wiki/000-Wiki_Guidance/004-Audit_Workflow/PAGE.md).
The links identify this installed package; another assigned Wiki requires its
own verified absolute procedure paths, not an assumed machine substitution.

## Original coverage and settled source identity

Before edits, record original integration scope and approved intent, accepted
repair evidence, target and ordered source full commit IDs, actual source root,
owned index/worktree fingerprints and relevant dirty/untracked bytes. Review
the actual candidate rather than assuming merged target, HEAD and working tree
are identical. For a range, resolve explicit before/after refs and inventory
adds, changes, renames (both paths) and deletes. Current-state scope instead
names subjects and hashes without inventing a comparison baseline.

Start with source changes and `metadata.source-files`, then inspect entry points,
unchanged callers/consumers, persistence and user-visible behavior. Search prose
and adjacent articles beyond metadata for affected claims, contradictions, new
capabilities and missing coverage. Record a subject/claim map with source path,
exact revision/hash or absence, supporting behavior, article path/hash or
missing-article finding, current statement, approved intent and limits. Empty
source lists may be valid guidance; an absent article needs a supported finding,
not a guessed page. Comments, test names and declared config are investigation
leads; distinguish source inspection, tests read and tests actually run.

Give every subject a disposition with reason/evidence: repair, retain unchanged,
consolidate, retire or unresolved. Name canonical fact owners. Consolidation or
retirement accounts for every useful material claim's successor or supported
obsolete disposition, all incoming links and history relocation. The Supervisor
settles ambiguous facts or returns the exact intent/prerequisite hold; it does
not dispatch an unapproved implementation to make documentation true.

Freeze exact supporting source and current page hashes before the editor starts,
including explicit absence for deleted sources/new pages. Immediately before
each replacement, reread the page and supporting source dependencies. Drift
requires coordination and bounded factual/coverage recheck, affected tests and
new current-byte evidence. Retain unaffected evidence; never overwrite a newer
page or merely relabel an old review's manifest. No factual baseline scanner,
freshness database or Wiki CLI relocation is part of this procedure.

## Leaf article editing and integrity

The editor receives exact writable articles/blocks, manager/report path,
original coverage, settled evidence, finding IDs and inactive overlapping writer
proof. It is not alone; preserve others' bytes and return conflicts to the
manager. No product code, runtime state, template copies or unrelated articles
are writable. Keep reports in the integration job, outside Wiki navigation.

Before a substantive rewrite, copy the **complete exact current PAGE.md bytes**
to adjacent `.versions/YYYY-MM-DD-HHMMSS.md` using local time. Create exclusively;
if that second already exists, use an unused suffix such as `-01.md`, never
overwrite an earlier snapshot. Hash/read back the copy before replacement;
failure to preserve the preimage prevents the edit. Recheck page/source bytes
after capture. Never version a `.versions/` file. New pages record absence;
byte-preserving moves retain timestamp and complete adjacent history. Typo and
generated-block-only changes need no version unless also substantively rewritten.

Keep implemented source-backed facts, approved future direction and open choices
distinct. Article lifecycle describes durable behavior; operational phase,
review verdict, job identity and temporary SPEC details belong in reports.
Preserve useful specialist facts, readable unwrapped prose, heading-article
ownership (`000-` child means no folder-level PAGE.md) and live cross-links.

Use nonempty `name`/`description`, exact unique repository-relative **code file**
paths in `metadata.source-files` (no directories/globs/absolute paths/plans),
or `[]` for no direct code subject with rationale. Resolve machine placeholders
explicitly; record unknown/deferred/external sources honestly. Remove legacy
relationship/connected-skill/trigger metadata on edited pages, preserving other
domain-owned metadata. Validate sources exist and own the claimed behavior.
Set quoted `metadata.last-modified: "YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:ssZ"` from actual UTC
write time on new/changed pages, including metadata, typo and imported generated
changes. Untouched review, no-op generation, timestamp-only refresh and
byte-preserving moves retain bytes/time. Never fabricate old timestamps or stamp
snapshots. Modification time supplies no factual verification evidence.

## Staged generated navigation

Only when structure/navigation changes, copy the intended Wiki to a disposable
Wiki directory and run the existing command with its explicit absolute path:

```sh
node <repository_root>/fusion-studio-server/scripts/wiki.js audit <disposable-Wiki>
```

Record exact command, tool/source hashes, before/after page hashes, raw results
and reviewed block differences. It writes `.audit-state.json` and may create
legacy TOC pages; it does not fact-check or stamp authored edit timestamps.
Import only intended script-owned `section-toc`/`children` blocks into their
recorded current pages; preserve hand-written prose and unrelated pages.
Do not hand-author those blocks or import `.audit-state.json`, hidden run records
or a whole staged tree. Explicitly assigned newly generated navigation pages
require normalizing metadata/heading ownership and recording absent preimage;
unexpected legacy pages are not automatically adopted. Stamp only actual
imported changes, then validate local links, metadata, sources and repeat
generation stability; a no-op retains page/time. `skipped (no-markers)` is normal
for an article without generated navigation.

Guide structure/coverage changes require the existing separate
[Sync Wiki Context](../../../../../Wiki/008-Workflows/001-Sync_Wiki_Context/PAGE.md)
procedure with its read-only research and accountable Guide writer. Ordinary
article fixes do not invoke it. The Supervisor assigns or holds that affected
work explicitly; this bounded editor cannot silently broaden into Guide refresh.

## Separate fresh documentation gate

The editor self-checks actual files and returns `READY_FOR_HANDOFF_REVIEW` with
the [job template](job-template.md) evidence fields. The Supervisor supplies a
different fresh read-only reviewer original scope/authority and current raw
source/page/check evidence, with no author conversation or prior diagnoses.
The reviewer independently builds coverage before reconciling writer reports;
checks original omissions, relevant retained/missing articles, renames/deletes,
factual accuracy, current/future/open distinctions, fact destinations, links,
exact sources, preimages, timestamps and generated-state exclusion.

Preserve each raw audit and actual reviewer identity/root inheritance/lifecycle;
record separate complete/partial/stale status and clean/findings/insufficient-
evidence assessment. Stable material findings follow manager-consolidated repair
and a new fresh gate on current dependent bytes plus omission/integration scope.
Stop at first materially clean pass. The manager records `HANDOFF_VALIDATED`
only with required checks and matching final source/page dependencies, including
retained pages; source/page drift invalidates affected acceptance. Missing
evidence/reviewer leaves `unmet-gate`. Documentation acceptance feeds the final
whole-candidate review; it certifies no app runtime, landing, adoption or Git act.
